  "notes": "{遠|とお}く is the ku-form of the i-adjective {遠|とお}い (far). It functions as both a noun meaning 'a distant place' and an adverb meaning 'far away.'\n\nPARTICLE PATTERNS:\n- {遠|とお}くに: in the distance (location)\n- {遠|とお}くから: from far away (origin)\n- {遠|とお}くへ/に: to a far place (direction)\n- {遠|とお}くまで: all the way to a distant place\n\nGRAMMAR NOTE:\nThis is a common pattern with i-adjectives: the く form can serve as both an adverb and a noun.\n- {近|ちか}い → {近|ちか}く: nearby\n- {高|たか}い → {高|たか}く: high (adverb)\n- {早|はや}い → {早|はや}く: early, quickly\n\nCONTRAST:\nOpposite of {近|ちか}く (nearby, a nearby place).",
